laurel 3030: the PM6125 PON watchdog ("PMIC WD") armed for the whole run: no pet for 60 s + 2 s = a hard reset by the PMIC, with no CPU and no TrustZone (the APSS bite gave no reset here, 2026-11-03 18:48). Petted by the APSS watchdog thread on its rule (every CPU answered), by the USB panic hold loop while it runs (17:56:16: a hold that went silent for 44 min now ends in a reset), and by the timed reset. Disarmed before every reset and power off of ours. Takes over the count the boot loader arms (mu 0202). Line LAUREL PMIC WDOG: on|off: REASON; kill switch laurelpmicwdog=0. Both kernels. docs/laurel_sprout/watchdog.md section 15.

